# Oplus CameraUnit SDK compat patch - SELinux rules
# (author: Paras Moharle)
#
# WHY
# ---
# With persist.sys.camera.private.log.enable=true the camera writes a private
# log to /data/vendor/cam_alog_<timestamp>.txt.  On this firmware the camera
# app (domain opluscamera_app) is not allowed to write there, so the writer
# fails and retries in a tight loop:
#
#   E/APS_ALOG: Failed to open directory
#   E/APS_ALOG: Unable to open file. Please disable SELinux and restart camerahalserver. !!!
#   E/APS_ALOG: CAM_ALOG_LIMIT, re-create file!
#
# That loop produced ~3000 log lines per second, pegged one CPU core, flooded
# the logcat buffer (other logs were dropped) and eventually got the camera
# process killed - which is exactly the "the camera works for a while and then
# it does not" behaviour.
#
# These two rules let the writer open the file.  They are policy rules only:
# no file label is changed and setenforce is never touched, so MediaTek's MKP
# kernel-integrity module cannot be provoked into a kernel panic.
#
# If the private log is switched off (persist.sys.camera.private.log.enable
# false) these rules are simply unused.
allow opluscamera_app vendor_data_file dir { add_name write open read search getattr }
allow opluscamera_app vendor_data_file file { create open write read getattr unlink setattr }
